.TH dalgon-dev-run 1  "dalgon-dev-run " 
.SH NAME
dalgon\-dev\-run \- Drive a scripted headless session from a scenario file (one step JSON per line).
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdalgon dev run\fR [\fB\-\-keep\fR] [\fB\-\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-consent\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFILE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Drive a scripted headless session from a scenario file (one step JSON per line).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\fR
Keep the run\*(Aqs data root and workspace for inspection
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Reuse an earlier kept run root instead of building a fresh one, so `resume` and `continue` session steps find a populated store
.TP
\fB\-\-consent\fR
Permit in\-band authorization: `run` and `answer` steps, `set_approval`, an `expect.request` answer, or a config\-declared `approval` act with the operator\*(Aqs privileges, so the scenario file alone cannot grant them
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIFILE\fR>
The scenario file: one step JSON object per nonblank line
